WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.512
The paper makes three contributions.

00:00:03.592 --> 00:00:07.103
First, it proposes DRAGONN,

00:00:07.183 --> 00:00:10.695
a hashing-based sparsification algorithm that
slashes compression overhead while keeping

00:00:10.775 --> 00:00:14.287
the same per-iteration convergence,

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:17.878
backed by theoretical bounds on both compression
error and generalization error.

00:00:17.958 --> 00:00:21.470
Second,

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:25.062
it adds two system-level optimizations: an
efficiency-aware tensor selection that only

00:00:25.142 --> 00:00:28.653
compresses tensors where it actually pays off,

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:32.245
and a sparse decoding scheme that keeps decode cost
from growing with the number of GPUs.

00:00:32.325 --> 00:00:35.837
Third,

00:00:35.917 --> 00:00:39.428
it evaluates the method broadly across vision and
recommendation models and demonstrates

00:00:39.508 --> 00:00:43.020
substantial end-to-end training speedups.
